      "writtenOn": "2016-07-15T23:39:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so. Playing with a device, I see two copies of the process name. Copy (1) is in /proc/$PID/cmdline, which I believe this line sets. It is not subject to the 16-character limit. Copy (2) is in /proc/$PID/stat, where, as I understand, pthread_setname_np() writes to through /proc/$PID/comm. This one is limited to 16 characters.\n\nI straced ps and it reads (1) first, falling back to (2) if there is nothing in cmdline. This explains how it can print \"com.google.android.apps...\" which is much longer than 16 characters. Accessing /proc/$PID/comm on an app process shows a truncated name.",
      "parentUuid": "5acfc472_7749d41d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 422,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 422,
        "endChar": 46
      },
